WEBVTT

00:06.810 --> 00:11.350
<i>We have an update on the plant robberies 
taking place all over the planet.</i>

00:11.780 --> 00:17.370
<i>Sources say the stolen plants 
are being transported to JuLai.</i>

00:17.370 --> 00:22.300
<i>The JuLai government is denying 
all allegations of involvement.</i>

00:22.300 --> 00:24.470
<i>The investigation is ongoing.</i>

00:42.730 --> 00:46.270
<i>My tears scattered like bits of paper</i>

00:46.270 --> 00:49.980
<i>Scared of the unknowable tomorrow</i>

00:49.980 --> 00:53.500
<i>I lived the same day over and over,
 back and forth</i>

00:53.500 --> 00:57.330
<i>But a new morning never came</i>

00:57.330 --> 00:59.580
<i>All the reasons to calm down</i>

00:59.580 --> 01:04.010
<i>Are just some moments until the crash</i>

01:04.530 --> 01:07.510
<i>I'm no longer the one that everyone knows</i>

01:07.510 --> 01:11.810
<i>Took off the fragile armor</i>

01:11.810 --> 01:18.880
<i>I don't want to lose any more love</i>

01:19.300 --> 01:26.360
<i>I don't want to lose any more love</i>

01:26.360 --> 01:30.050
<i>There's still no line 
between today and tomorrow</i>

01:30.050 --> 01:33.620
<i>My waking nightmare doesn't end</i>

01:33.620 --> 01:37.250
<i>And yet I won't lose hope</i>

01:37.250 --> 01:43.300
<i>And yet there's no night that doesn't end</i>

01:43.300 --> 01:55.640
<i>Not here, not here</i>

01:59.380 --> 02:01.880
Who will benefit this planet more? Humans?

02:01.880 --> 02:03.650
Or plants?

02:04.180 --> 02:05.810
Which do you think?

02:05.810 --> 02:08.260
Whose side are you on?

02:08.260 --> 02:11.450
Humans really like
 dividing things into groups.

02:12.470 --> 02:17.490
The Worms take no sides. 
We <i>are</i> the planet.

02:19.170 --> 02:20.870
Here's what Knives thinks...

02:21.530 --> 02:25.120
You greedy humans aren't capable 
of using plants correctly.

02:25.620 --> 02:26.910
In fact,

02:26.910 --> 02:31.650
you'll devour them just like you 
did your previous planet, Earth.

02:32.820 --> 02:35.380
You know about the Last Run, don't you?

02:35.910 --> 02:39.340
Is that why you're gathering red plants?

02:39.340 --> 02:42.300
Better than wasting them, don't you think?

02:42.730 --> 02:47.530
So, humans or plants? 
Which will benefit this planet more?

02:47.530 --> 02:50.220
I know we can't keep going the way we are.

02:50.220 --> 02:53.620
There are people raising flora,
 a replacement for plants.

02:53.620 --> 02:55.490
You mean Luida.

02:55.490 --> 02:59.330
Luida is a geoplant specialist.

02:59.330 --> 03:03.620
I'm sure she's pursuing her own way of
 saving the human race on this planet.

03:03.620 --> 03:05.650
I am doing the same.

03:05.650 --> 03:09.220
You are? That's not the impression I got.

03:10.290 --> 03:11.360
Follow me.

03:18.280 --> 03:19.740
Where do you think you're going?

03:19.740 --> 03:21.120
You're not coming?

03:21.860 --> 03:25.380
Is there a clearance sale 
on your life or something?

03:25.380 --> 03:28.720
This is our chance to find out 
what Millions Knives is after.

03:32.140 --> 03:34.780
Stolen from right under my nose...

03:41.300 --> 03:43.210
This is JuLai...

03:45.210 --> 03:47.280
It's changed quite a bit.

03:52.020 --> 03:53.980
JuLai, the third city...

03:54.870 --> 03:57.310
A fortified metropolis, 
largest of the seven cities.

03:58.600 --> 04:01.380
Thanks to her monopoly 
on water-producing plants,

04:01.990 --> 04:04.310
she can buy up all the bullets she wants.

04:06.940 --> 04:08.530
I'd call her opulent.

04:26.160 --> 04:27.290
You dipshit!

04:28.240 --> 04:30.200
I remember you!

04:31.070 --> 04:32.490
Hey! Hold it!

04:33.210 --> 04:35.460
Stop it! Stop right there!

04:43.630 --> 04:45.760
Halt! Or I'll shoot!

04:48.050 --> 04:50.720
That's right. Be good little boys.

04:52.350 --> 04:54.480
All right, Officer...

04:54.960 --> 04:57.310
What'd we do to deserve this?

04:57.310 --> 05:00.360
Don't play dumb! He's the Humanoid Typhoon.

05:00.360 --> 05:02.570
Are you here to destroy this city, too?!

05:02.570 --> 05:05.950
I won't let you turn JuLai 
into the next Jeneora Rock!

05:08.130 --> 05:10.120
Don't do it, Wolfwood.

05:10.850 --> 05:12.870
Is now really the time for that?

05:12.870 --> 05:16.700
My parents were in 
Jeneora Rock when it happened.

05:17.300 --> 05:20.130
And you... How could you?

05:23.090 --> 05:24.670
Hey, Needle-noggin!

05:25.980 --> 05:27.490
Hey! Are you okay?!

05:27.490 --> 05:30.010
I-I-I didn't give the order to shoot!

05:30.010 --> 05:31.690
Put a sock in it, asshole!

05:31.690 --> 05:32.710
Okay!

05:32.710 --> 05:33.650
Tch...

05:33.650 --> 05:34.980
Let's go.

05:34.990 --> 05:36.250
Hey, Needle-noggin!

05:40.290 --> 05:41.110
After them!

05:46.180 --> 05:51.880
You must have seen the flora and thought, 
"What a wonderful breakthrough."

05:51.880 --> 05:52.890
I did.

05:52.890 --> 05:56.800
But that plan would take an 
extraordinarily long time to implement.

05:56.800 --> 06:00.040
Are you certain mankind
 would survive until then?

06:02.540 --> 06:06.760
Luida's ambition of changing 
the environment is admirable.

06:06.760 --> 06:09.510
But time is of the essence.

06:09.510 --> 06:12.040
We don't have the luxury 
of exploring alternatives.

06:12.040 --> 06:14.720
And so what's your answer, then?

06:17.380 --> 06:18.780
Humanity.

06:19.440 --> 06:23.440
#10 Humanity

06:26.610 --> 06:28.470
Requiring neither food nor drink,

06:28.470 --> 06:31.240
capable of withstanding the 
temperature differential of the desert...

06:31.240 --> 06:33.780
My goal was a new breed of humanity.

06:34.420 --> 06:37.290
You... operate on people here?

06:37.290 --> 06:39.290
You've seen them.

06:39.870 --> 06:41.910
E. G. the Mine.

06:41.910 --> 06:43.750
Monev the Gale.

06:43.750 --> 06:45.640
Livio the Double Fang.

06:46.050 --> 06:48.210
And Nicholas.

06:48.210 --> 06:50.560
What? The undertaker?

06:50.560 --> 06:53.970
Yes, Nicholas the Punisher.

06:54.570 --> 06:57.740
He, too, is my creation.

06:59.940 --> 07:03.660
Hanging around you is gonna get me killed.

07:04.110 --> 07:05.270
Sorry.

07:05.270 --> 07:09.340
You turn into a deer the moment
 you're up against humans.

07:09.340 --> 07:12.170
I'm sorry. But thank you.

07:12.170 --> 07:12.780
Huh?

07:13.530 --> 07:15.780
You didn't kill them.

07:15.780 --> 07:19.150
How could I? You took off without me.

07:21.380 --> 07:23.450
Get yourself patched up already!

07:23.450 --> 07:25.430
Or are you gonna fart around till you pass out?

07:26.390 --> 07:27.600
Got it.

07:32.400 --> 07:33.260
Needle-noggin...

07:35.730 --> 07:37.570
Those scars...

07:37.570 --> 07:40.280
Oh, how embarrassing.

07:41.100 --> 07:42.100
Ow...

07:42.830 --> 07:45.400
So that's the price you pay
 for saving everyone.

07:46.360 --> 07:54.490
It's not hard to imagine how people 
have treated an aberration like you.

07:55.010 --> 07:58.130
I can't understand why you want
 to help humans so much.

07:58.130 --> 07:59.480
How do you even put up with 'em?

08:01.150 --> 08:04.160
My body moves before I can think.

08:05.210 --> 08:07.460
I can't abandon anyone who's in tight spot.

08:09.080 --> 08:10.170
That includes you.

08:12.360 --> 08:14.420
So you figured me out.

08:16.720 --> 08:21.760
Did you think sacrificing yourself 
will make everyone happy?

08:23.410 --> 08:24.640
How awful...

08:25.210 --> 08:30.040
They were all doomed to
 die of illness or poverty.

08:30.810 --> 08:36.380
I saved lives and gave purpose to
 ordinary folk who had none.

08:36.840 --> 08:40.480
You kidnapped orphans and
 sick people to toy with them.

08:40.480 --> 08:41.750
He's right!

08:41.750 --> 08:44.870
I did nothing to demean them!

08:44.870 --> 08:49.490
Yeah, I bet. You seem even
 more uptight than you look.

08:50.020 --> 08:51.420
Want a sip?

08:54.070 --> 08:59.180
My surgeries helped make them tougher.

08:59.650 --> 09:04.830
But that was all.
They still hungered and thirsted.

09:04.830 --> 09:06.060
They were failures.

09:08.450 --> 09:14.570
Nothing like Millions Knives, 
the Independent plant...

09:16.710 --> 09:19.590
The ultimate life-form.

09:33.830 --> 09:38.690
So if we cannot patch people together,
we must alter them before birth.

09:41.410 --> 09:47.050
Thus, with help from Knives and
 the study of lab-grown clones,

09:48.430 --> 09:49.780
we created this child.

09:55.270 --> 09:57.260
How could you...

09:57.260 --> 10:02.270
But its power level is only
 around that of a supply gate.

10:02.700 --> 10:04.790
The child neither human nor plant.

10:05.640 --> 10:10.090
But can't you see these kids
 <i>are</i> already born?

10:10.790 --> 10:14.100
I just want you to understand...

10:14.680 --> 10:18.420
that this is for the future
 of mankind on this planet.

10:19.550 --> 10:21.600
What arrogance...

10:21.600 --> 10:26.600
If that's what you think, young lady,
 you may kill me right here and now.

10:27.580 --> 10:32.570
You will get what you want 
and save a few lives, yes.

10:32.570 --> 10:36.650
But at the same time, 
you'll be killing countless possibilities.

10:39.030 --> 10:44.000
Both Knives and I are looking 
much further ahead into the future.

10:44.000 --> 10:47.480
It's a lonely job, but it must be done.

10:49.150 --> 10:53.940
For the sake of creating a new
 human race, I would pay any price.

10:53.940 --> 10:57.240
Even if that must be one of the twins.

10:57.240 --> 11:01.390
Nonsense. You think you're
 gonna save the world?

11:01.910 --> 11:07.270
What's more important than how you feel
 seeing these kids right here in front of you?

11:07.930 --> 11:09.320
I pity them...

11:14.720 --> 11:18.180
Who are you to pity me?

11:34.750 --> 11:36.780
That's why I hate humans.

11:37.290 --> 11:40.530
You only ever judge by what <i>you</i> can see.

11:40.530 --> 11:42.340
Stop it, Elendira!

11:42.340 --> 11:43.440
Silence!

11:44.570 --> 11:46.010
H-Hey!

11:54.930 --> 11:56.020
Wow, it worked.

11:56.480 --> 11:57.660
What did I tell you?!

11:57.660 --> 11:59.030
I'm sorry!

11:59.030 --> 12:01.410
Always sticking your nose into trouble...

12:01.410 --> 12:02.650
I'm sorry!

12:02.650 --> 12:06.100
If I get hurt and worker's comp 
doesn't cover it, you're on the hook!

12:07.060 --> 12:10.330
I'm sorry!

12:14.940 --> 12:17.040
That doc is crazy.

12:17.520 --> 12:21.230
This is a trap. 
They're trying to lure Vash here.

12:21.550 --> 12:23.670
We have to let him know!

12:25.610 --> 12:27.860
Please hurry! Hurry!

12:38.900 --> 12:40.860
Found you.

12:49.550 --> 12:53.790
Oh, no! You would kill a
 pitiful creature like me?

12:53.790 --> 12:57.540
How cruel! Horrible! Awful!

12:58.210 --> 13:01.100
See? Always judging by looks.

13:01.100 --> 13:03.720
You're all driven by discrimination.

13:03.720 --> 13:05.470
You monster.

13:05.470 --> 13:09.100
Monster? Did you just call me a monster?

13:09.640 --> 13:13.600
You should really... speak for yourself.

13:17.030 --> 13:18.610
We're almost there.

13:18.610 --> 13:21.110
Just gotta survive until the elevator comes.

13:21.110 --> 13:22.500
Huh?

13:22.500 --> 13:24.980
We run on the count of three.

13:24.980 --> 13:27.460
One, two...

13:27.980 --> 13:29.070
Three!

13:47.090 --> 13:47.910
Vash?!

13:47.910 --> 13:49.260
Quickly now, you two!

13:49.260 --> 13:51.350
Took you long enough!

13:52.200 --> 13:54.030
Punisher!

13:59.910 --> 14:02.080
Jeez, talk about in the nick of time.

14:02.080 --> 14:04.880
Phew, we're safe. But how did you...

14:04.880 --> 14:06.780
Call it a hunch.

14:08.620 --> 14:11.740
Don't go, Vash! It's a trap!

14:18.210 --> 14:23.340
Ouch! Ow, ow, ow, ow, ow, ow!

14:23.340 --> 14:25.750
Oh, the pain...

14:26.730 --> 14:29.090
That's pathetic, you dummy.

14:29.090 --> 14:30.920
I hate you!

14:30.920 --> 14:34.930
Well, the feeling's mutual. 
Maybe we'll get along after all.

14:34.930 --> 14:39.860
We will not, you jerk! Just get out of here.

14:39.860 --> 14:41.640
Yeah, yeah.

14:41.640 --> 14:43.260
Does it hurt?

14:43.260 --> 14:44.290
Your injury...

14:44.290 --> 14:46.150
Don't touch me, scum!

14:46.150 --> 14:50.670
You traitor! You don't even 
know how much Lord Knives...

14:55.390 --> 14:57.250
Hey, Needle-noggin!

14:57.250 --> 15:00.370
Leave the little creep alone. Let's scram.

15:00.880 --> 15:04.380
Come on, Roberto! 
We have to go after them and...

15:12.330 --> 15:13.920
Goodness gracious...

15:18.150 --> 15:20.190
Looks like I messed up.

15:20.730 --> 15:21.840
No!

15:23.710 --> 15:27.210
Maybe I had a bit too much to drink.

15:27.810 --> 15:30.910
Keep your hands to yourself.
 It hurts enough.

15:30.910 --> 15:33.110
But... But the bleeding...

15:34.670 --> 15:36.760
Pass me my booze.

15:36.760 --> 15:39.160
This is no time for that!

15:40.070 --> 15:42.790
Will you <i>ever</i> get off my case? Good grief.

15:43.630 --> 15:47.040
If I drink, it might just come
out the hole in my gut.

15:50.080 --> 15:52.740
This is all my fault...

15:53.780 --> 15:55.180
Yeah.

15:56.170 --> 15:59.430
You limited what I can drink, so...

16:01.440 --> 16:06.450
Damn, my head's too clear for this.

16:09.820 --> 16:11.030
Take this.

16:12.450 --> 16:15.580
No! I can't leave you!

16:15.580 --> 16:20.120
You listen here. 
You're in charge from now on.

16:20.120 --> 16:21.470
Follow your heart.

16:21.470 --> 16:22.770
No.

16:22.770 --> 16:26.140
You can run if you want. Well?

16:29.420 --> 16:31.460
Meryl Stryfe.

16:37.580 --> 16:43.390
I... was just unlucky...

16:56.590 --> 16:58.140
I'm sorry...

17:19.310 --> 17:22.520
Not wanting to kill anyone...

17:22.930 --> 17:25.860
That's just a coward's idealism.

17:25.860 --> 17:28.020
Even a kid could tell you that.

17:29.150 --> 17:34.250
Folks only get to live 
'cause other people die.

17:34.250 --> 17:36.030
That's the world we live in.

17:38.610 --> 17:43.200
I don't have the luxury of being 
afraid to make tough decisions.

17:44.940 --> 17:46.610
I have to choose.

17:47.540 --> 17:50.910
In order to protect 
the things that are dear to me.

17:53.330 --> 17:55.550
So I'll do anything I have to.

17:56.550 --> 17:58.460
As a guide.

17:59.220 --> 18:00.920
For the orphanage?

18:02.480 --> 18:05.220
What a load of babysitting 
this job turned out to be.

18:05.220 --> 18:09.340
Dragging someone so eager to die 
all the way out here alive...

18:10.040 --> 18:11.730
But it's done now.

18:11.730 --> 18:13.050
Wolfwood.

18:14.510 --> 18:16.160
Thanks for everything.

19:02.220 --> 19:04.620
One of our brethren from back then.

19:04.620 --> 19:06.600
I keep her here as a warning for myself.

19:07.580 --> 19:12.020
The humans aren't exploiting 
them because they want to.

19:12.890 --> 19:15.090
What did you come all the way out here for?

19:15.460 --> 19:17.380
To take back the plants.

19:21.690 --> 19:23.010
And not just that.

19:23.470 --> 19:28.160
The rash of robberies everywhere...
That was you, Nai, wasn't it?

19:28.160 --> 19:29.810
What an accusation.

19:31.140 --> 19:35.850
All I'm doing is rescuing our brethren who've
been discriminated against and oppressed.

19:35.850 --> 19:39.030
We can coexist with humans too, Nai!

19:39.030 --> 19:40.750
Vash!

19:41.660 --> 19:46.460
You don't want to save the humans 
because you love them.

19:47.790 --> 19:51.500
You just want to make up for 
causing the crash 150 years ago.

19:54.300 --> 19:57.650
Your contract is complete. Take this.

19:59.500 --> 20:03.090
What good is this piece 
of paper supposed to do?

20:03.770 --> 20:09.570
I'll never forget what 
you did to me. Or to Livio.

20:12.720 --> 20:16.930
Nicholas, were you able
 to lay down your cross?

20:18.250 --> 20:19.570
What about you?

20:31.030 --> 20:32.750
I can't believe it! Nai?!

20:32.750 --> 20:37.800
You survived the crash... the Big Fall?

20:39.820 --> 20:44.720
Long time no see, 
Count Lebnant Vasques. Or should I say...

20:44.720 --> 20:46.800
Researcher Bill Conrad?

20:48.580 --> 20:53.890
You choose. Join the trash heap of
 hundreds of thousands perished...

20:54.660 --> 20:57.520
Or live and atone for the
 Sinners' transgressions.

20:58.830 --> 21:00.660
Where did those eyes...

21:00.660 --> 21:02.030
Forgive me.

21:02.980 --> 21:07.980
What I have done to you...
 cannot be undone...

21:12.620 --> 21:15.540
My atonement is unending.

21:15.540 --> 21:20.370
No matter how much you try to atone, 
the humans will never forgive you.

21:20.870 --> 21:23.440
No matter how much you fool yourself,

21:23.440 --> 21:27.090
in their eyes, you're still a monster.

21:28.140 --> 21:31.950
I know humans make sacrifices
 in order to live,

21:32.390 --> 21:35.070
but they're trying to move forward.

21:35.070 --> 21:37.350
I want to believe in them.

21:38.030 --> 21:41.860
I feel sorry for you. You're sick.

21:42.230 --> 21:44.930
I'll put you out of your misery.

21:58.780 --> 22:00.690
I will remake you.

22:02.340 --> 22:04.180
To be more like me...

22:04.180 --> 22:06.800
The perfect Independent!

22:08.970 --> 22:10.470
Don't, Nai!

22:17.390 --> 22:20.060
All shall be even again.

22:20.060 --> 22:27.680
<i>Your light...</i>

22:34.140 --> 22:38.440
<i>If that light never changes</i>

22:38.440 --> 22:42.870
<i>And continues to shine high above the sky</i>

22:42.870 --> 22:47.180
<i>Even when I'm lost, 
even when I'm struggling</i>

22:47.180 --> 22:51.430
<i>I'll continue to search for you</i>

22:51.430 --> 22:55.720
<i>Even on days of sickness or sadness</i>

22:55.720 --> 23:00.100
<i>I'll open the window to a new morning</i>

23:00.100 --> 23:04.290
<i>I'm moving forward, I'm standing still</i>

23:04.290 --> 23:07.850
<i>Tell the people who are praying</i>

23:07.850 --> 23:13.810
<i>But today this flower 
before me is praising you</i>

23:13.810 --> 23:16.820
<i>My song is a song of joy and wishes</i>

23:16.820 --> 23:19.540
<i>Yes, I'm reaching out</i>

23:19.540 --> 23:24.880
<i>But you're too high up 
in the evening stars</i>

23:24.880 --> 23:30.850
<i>But today this flower 
before me is praising you</i>

23:30.850 --> 23:34.000
<i>My song is a song of joy and wishes</i>

23:34.000 --> 23:36.700
<i>Yes, I try to reach out</i>

23:36.700 --> 23:41.860
<i>But you're too high up 
in the evening stars</i>
